From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] python: guard the simsense import when CUDA is disabled

Upstream-Status: To upstream [affects every non-CUDA Linux build, not riscv64-specific]

Real riscv64 CI (this PR's run, job 133890774516): the wheel builds and
installs fine, but the import smoke test fails outright:

    ImportError: cannot import name 'simsense' from 'sapien.pysapien'

CMakeLists.txt's own SAPIEN_CUDA option (default ON, forced OFF by this
port's setup.py when CUDA_PATH is unset - no riscv64 CUDA toolkit exists)
gates `add_subdirectory("3rd_party/simsense")` directly, so a CUDA-less
build never compiles that extension module into pysapien at all. But
py_package/__init__.py's own import of it is only guarded against macOS
(`if platform.system() != "Darwin":`), not against a CUDA-disabled Linux
build - upstream never ships a Linux wheel with CUDA off, so this gap
has no prior opportunity to surface.

Also check that the compiled module actually exposes simsense before
importing it, same shape as the existing Darwin check, rather than
assuming every non-Darwin build has it.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 python/py_package/__init__.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/python/py_package/__init__.py b/python/py_package/__init__.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/python/py_package/__init__.py
+++ b/python/py_package/__init__.py
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 from .pysapien import math

 import platform
-if platform.system() != "Darwin":
+if platform.system() != "Darwin" and hasattr(pysapien, "simsense"):
     from .pysapien import simsense

 from . import physx
